    description: "FILED 2026-10-01 from WI-mofil-tidog-forob-tovah-givud-lijog-vuvug-gutid's per-module slot A/B.\n\nMECHANISM. INV-kotob refuses a PROJECT type in the swift module slot (it rides only in receiver_type_hint). Two kinds of name escape that refusal and fill the slot as if external:\n  (1) a GENERIC TYPE PARAMETER used as a declared type -- `func secureCompare<C>(to other: C)`, `init(..., downstream: Downstream)` with `Inner<Downstream: Subscriber>`: the parameter arm (`_swift_param_name_and_type`) and the field registry take the spelling `C` / `Downstream` / `T` as a type. `_swift_type_parameter_names` already exists and is applied to RETURN types (WI-higob), not to parameter or property annotations.\n  (2) a NESTED project type spelled with a dot -- `MemoryStorage.Backend`, `DiskStorage.Backend` (Kingfisher), `URLEncodedFormNode.Array` / `.Map` (hummingbird), `URLEncodedFormEncoder.Configuration` (vapor), `URLEncodedFormEncoder.DateEncoding` etc. (Alamofire): the project-type test does not recognise the dotted name.\n\nCOUNTED (analyze_swift, external method edges by dst module, dev 8cfcab7b07 = BEFORE WI-mofil):\n  vapor:       T 10, C 8, URLEncodedFormEncoder.Configuration 5, Element 2, E 2, Base 1\n  hummingbird: URLEncodedFormNode.Array 7, URLEncodedFormNode.Map 5, ChildChannel 4, Base 2, Context 1\n  Kingfisher:  MemoryStorage.Backend 59, DiskStorage.Backend 58, Base 32, T 2\n  Alamofire:   Downstream 12, Failure 2, T 1\n  swift-argument-parser: T 12\nAfter WI-mofil's branch: hummingbird URLEncodedFormNode.Array 26 (+19), Kingfisher DiskStorage.Backend 63 (+5), Alamofire URLEncodedFormEncoder.* 9 (+9, new), vapor C 9 (+1); Downstream 12 -> 0 and ChildChannel 4 -> 3 (their leak sources closed). Only names on the list above were counted -- a full census needs the declared generic parameters and nested types per file, which this count does NOT do.\n\nWhy it matters: a filled slot names a catalogue MODULE; `T` / `C` / `Base` cannot match a row (harmless to recall) but a project nested type named like a library one could, and every such row inflates the \"slot filled\" measurement that receiver-typing work is priced on (WI-mofil's own +18 Kingfisher / +33 hummingbird gains include 5 / 19 of these).\n\nDIRECTION. Apply the generic-parameter filter wherever a declared type is read (parameter, property, if-let annotation, field registry); test the project-type refusal against the dotted name's HEAD as well as the full name."  # 7d26
    fields: {}  # 7d26
